  "_style": "Always address the user informally with «чи» (чиний, чамд, чамайг, чамтай; requests as soft informal imperatives «Бичээрэй», «Шалгаарай»), never «та» for the single user. For the couple together prefer «хоёулаа», «хамтдаа», «та хоёр» (the only acceptable plural form) or «бидний/манай» when the couple speaks. The other person is always «хань» / «хань чинь» (ханьдаа, ханьтайгаа, ханиасаа), which is gender-neutral; never залуу, охин, нөхөр, эхнэр, найз залуу/охин. Mongolian has no grammatical gender, so keep sentences neutral by avoiding gendered nouns. Quote marks: outer « », inner „ “; ellipsis is the single character …; dash — with spaces; no space before ! ? : ; and keep « · », emoji and \\n exactly as in the source. Numbers: non-breaking space as thousands separator (12 500), decimal comma (4,5), 24-hour time (21:30); dates as «11-р сарын 14» or «2026 оны 11-р сарын 14» (months are numbered, not named). Buttons and actions are short verbal nouns in -х form as in Mongolian iOS («Хадгалах», «Захидал битүүмжлэх», «Дахин оролдох»); titles, tabs, chips and buttons use sentence case (only the first word capitalized) except proper names such as Coupley, Premium and AI. Script: standard Mongolian Cyrillic with ө and ү, never replace them with о/у or with Latin letters; observe vowel harmony in suffixes. Plural categories are [\"one\",\"other\"]; a noun after a number stays singular, so both forms are usually identical («%lld өдөр», «%lld дурсамж»). A partner's name placeholder (%@) is never declined or suffixed (no «%@-д», «%@-ын», «%@-тай»): rephrase so the name stands alone in the nominative, e.g. «Хань чинь (%@) …» or «%@: …», or use «хань чинь» instead. Tone: warm, light, kind, never cheesy.",
